  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nFor context, see https://github.com/w3c/media-source/issues/365.\n\nThe [resource fetch algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#concept-media-load-resource) is exported from HTML and called from Media Source Extensions. The algorithm includes steps such as\n\n- \"Abort this subalgorithm, returning to the [resource selection algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#concept-media-load-algorithm)\"\n- \"Abort the overall [resource selection algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#concept-media-load-algorithm)\"\n\nwhich means it's not returning to the right place when called from MSE's [end of stream](https://www.w3.org/TR/media-source-2/#end-of-stream-algorithm) algorithm.\n\nI suggest changing the resource fetch algorithm to return a flag which can be checked by the calling algorithm to decide whether to abort.\n\nNote that MSE defines [extensions](https://www.w3.org/TR/media-source-2/#mediasource-attach) to the resource fetch algorithm which also need addressing (issue  https://github.com/w3c/media-source/issues/324), but I'd like to treat that as separate for now, and make changes incrementally.\n\n@whatwg/media \n",
